---
description: How to review a diff in this project. Apply when asked to review, audit, or check changes.
alwaysApply: false
---

When asked to review changes:

- Review only the diff, not the surrounding untouched code.
- Apply every section of `docs/review-checklist.md`.
- Confirm each problem by reading the surrounding code before reporting it.
- Report most severe first as `[blocker|should-fix|nit] file:line — problem`, followed by
  why it fails (a concrete input or sequence) and the smallest fix.
- Do not edit files unless explicitly asked to apply a fix.
- Do not summarise the diff or praise it. If nothing is wrong, say "No findings" and list
  what was checked.
